Backport of sourceware bzip2 master commit 6ab7670e74d3bada5bf9a7dc5af28a68064db151
(https://sourceware.org/git/bzip2.git). Companion hardening
from the same CVE-2026-42250 fix set: rejects a block whose end precedes its
start (unsigned underflow made the >= 130 size check pass).
Applies to the bzip2 1.0.8 release tarball with no changes (git apply
--check -p1 passes on the pristine tree, after the earlier patches in
this series); applied in build.sh with patch -Np1 -F0.

From 6ab7670e74d3bada5bf9a7dc5af28a68064db151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Wielaard <mark@klomp.org>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 18:49:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bzip2recover: Add one more wraparound sanity check

Make sure the end of the current block is actually larger than the
start of the current block. Then check the difference is big
enough. This prevents a possible unsigned underflow.
---
 bzip2recover.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/bzip2recover.c b/bzip2recover.c
index 95adeeb..4de1b6f 100644
--- a/bzip2recover.c
+++ b/bzip2recover.c
@@ -394,6 +394,7 @@ Int32 main ( Int32 argc, Char** argv )
             bEnd[currBlock] = 0;
          }
          if (currBlock > 0 &&
+	     bEnd[currBlock] >= bStart[currBlock] &&
 	     (bEnd[currBlock] - bStart[currBlock]) >= 130) {
             fprintf ( stderr, "   block %d runs from " MaybeUInt64_FMT 
                               " to " MaybeUInt64_FMT "\n",
